# Mobile app (`src/`)

## Layers

| Layer | Path | May import |
|---|---|---|
| ui | `features/*/ui/` | application, domain, shared |
| application | `features/*/application/` | domain, data |
| domain | `features/*/domain/` | nothing from features/shared ui |
| data | `features/*/data/` | domain only |

## Navigation

- Tabs: `src/shared/navigation/MainTabNavigator.tsx`
- Create stack: `src/shared/navigation/CreateNavigator.tsx`
- Types: `src/shared/navigation/types.ts`
- New screens: add to stack + implement under `features/<feature>/ui/screens/`

## Shared UI

Reuse `src/shared/ui/Screen.tsx` and `Button.tsx`. Match wireframes in `docs-site/content/wireframes.md`.

## Create flow (current)

```
TemplatePicker → AddPhotos → Details → Preview → ShareSuccess
```

Draft state: `CreateDraftContext` / `useCreateDraft` in `application/`.

## Next implementation targets

- `features/create/data/creationRepository.ts`
- `features/create/data/uploadService.ts`
- `features/create/domain/quota.ts`

Wire through `application/` hooks — screens call hooks, not Firebase directly.

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — Firebase in screen
import firestore from '@react-native-firebase/firestore';

// ✅ GOOD — screen uses application hook
const { generateShareLink, isLoading } = useCreateShareLink();
```
